Resolve the build's own libpython through a run path on the build executables.

The build interpreter, Programs/_testembed and copies of the interpreter that
the test suite makes (venvs) must load the libpython of this build. Loader
environment variables are not used: LD_LIBRARY_PATH loses against the run
paths the EasyBuild RPATH wrappers add, and LD_PRELOAD is inherited by host
programs the tests start, which cannot load a libpython built against a newer
glibc than the host's.

The flag is spelled -Wl,-rpath=DIR on purpose. The RPATH wrappers place the
entries they recognise in command line order ahead of the directories they add
themselves, which under EESSI end with the compatibility layer's library
directory and its own libpython of the same soname. A run path passed as
-Wl,-rpath,DIR is not recognised and stays behind those. The easyconfig
removes the build directory from the installed run paths.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -7737,7 +7737,9 @@
     Linux*|GNU*|NetBSD*|FreeBSD*|DragonFly*|OpenBSD*|VxWorks*)
       LDLIBRARY='libpython$(LDVERSION).so'
       BLDLIBRARY='-L. -lpython$(LDVERSION)'
-      RUNSHARED=LD_LIBRARY_PATH=`pwd`${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}}
+      # Build executables resolve libpython without exporting loader settings.
+      RUNSHARED=''
+      LDFLAGS_NODIST="$LDFLAGS_NODIST -Wl,-rpath=$(pwd)"
 
       # The Android Gradle plugin will only package libraries whose names end
       # with ".so".

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1580,7 +1580,9 @@
     Linux*|GNU*|NetBSD*|FreeBSD*|DragonFly*|OpenBSD*|VxWorks*)
       LDLIBRARY='libpython$(LDVERSION).so'
       BLDLIBRARY='-L. -lpython$(LDVERSION)'
-      RUNSHARED=LD_LIBRARY_PATH=`pwd`${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}}
+      # Build executables resolve libpython without exporting loader settings.
+      RUNSHARED=''
+      LDFLAGS_NODIST="$LDFLAGS_NODIST -Wl,-rpath=$(pwd)"
 
       # The Android Gradle plugin will only package libraries whose names end
       # with ".so".
